oup in this case  think about the climate skeptic in your  investment team  or think about that voice who wants to  drive change but finds no ally in a  silent room  can you be that ally  or that disruptor  of a social norm  okay and then number three  for those of you sitting here  who want to run for office one day and i  would love to see it  you can engage with a stanford-funded  non-profit called climate cabinet  whose whole job is to  empower you and your staffers  with a knowledgeable  actionable  relevant and constituent-friendly  platform about climate  from how we produce power to how we grow  our food  to how we manufacture  and run our buildings  the possibilities are there  and i can feel it  in all of your hands  so let's come back  to the 2015 i had talked about  actually not the one i had talked about  but the one that we all want our  children to see  what do you want them to see  will it be blue skies  or orange  what is the air  that they smell  when they play soccer  or the water that they taste  at the end of a long day  i know that each of us all have an  important role to play  and from this day forward  we will be judged on the decisions we  make when it mattered  or the decisions we did not  together  we can all  employ civic engagement and our vote  to move the needle forward  for the future that we want to see  thank you  [Applause]  [Music]  you

